---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets'
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro'
import DataTable from '../../components/DataTable.astro'
import Location from '../../components/Location.astro'
import IconBoxArrowUpRight from '../../components/icons/IconBoxArrowUpRight.astro'
import { FORM_LINK } from '../../config/site'
import { templesByCountry } from '../../data/temples'
import logo from '../../assets/images/logo-monks-life.png'

/* Decorative banner, so it is a CSS background rather than an <img>. */
const banner = await getImage({ src: logo, width: 640, format: 'webp' })

const itinerary = {
  headers: ['Date', '&nbsp;&nbsp;Activity'],
  rows: [
    ['12-18 June', '&nbsp;&nbsp;First week of training'],
    ['12 June', '&nbsp;&nbsp;Registration'],
    ['15 June', '&nbsp;&nbsp;Ceremony of shaving the hair for the first time'],
    ['19 June', '&nbsp;&nbsp;Ordination day'],
    ['20-30 June', '&nbsp;&nbsp;Training continues'],
    ['1 July onwards', '&nbsp;&nbsp;Stay on as a monk at the Dhammakaya temple in your home country or in Belgium, dependent on assessment (optional)'],
  ],
}
---

<Base title="Program details - European Ordination Program">
  {/* Decorative banner: the navbar already carries the labelled logo. */}
  <div id="index-header" role="presentation" style={`background-image: url(${banner.src})`}></div>
  <div class="container">
    <p class="lead mt-5">
      While many are searching for peace outside, we believe that world peace MUST begin from each and everyone of us.
      That is why we promote the use of meditation in order to help individuals cultivate peace from within.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open to men of all ethnicities and backgrounds, the European Ordination Program provides the opportunity to
      learn about Buddhism and a monk's way of life. Taking part in the experience will aid in the cultivation of one's
      inner peace.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Dhammakaya Foundation is a non-profit organisation, based on personal development, aiming to promote activities
      for the restoration of morality in individuals, families, societies, and the world.
    </p>
    <div id="program-details--latest-news" class="offset-anchor-for-fixed-nav"></div>
    <h1 class="text-center mt-5">Latest news and announcements</h1>
    <p>
      <Location />
    </p>
    <DataTable table={itinerary} />
    <div id="program-details--what-is-the-european-ordination-program" class="offset-anchor-for-fixed-nav"></div>
    <h1 class="text-center mt-5">What is the European Ordination Program?</h1>
    <p>
      The European Ordination Program has been established by the vision of Luang Por Dhammajayo, the Abbot of Wat
      Phra Dhammakaya, to introduce Buddhism to the people in Europe, and others around the world. The
      program was organized for the first time in 2013 at Wat Phra Dhammakaya Belgium. Many participants in Europe
      from different countries such as England, Belgium, France, Germany, Sweden, Denmark, The Netherlands, Italy,
      Malta, Austria, and Switzerland joined the program. When it concluded, all were very satisfied with the program,
      and many had the intention to join the same program again the following year.
    </p>
    <p>
      The European committee, consisting of 29 branches of Wat Phra Dhammakaya decided to organise the program every year.
      Subsequently, more and more participants in Europe have joined and participated in the European Ordination Program.
    </p>
    <p>
      The European Ordination Program provides the opportunity for all qualified persons in Europe who have interest in
      studying the Dhamma of the Buddha, to use the knowledge they learn and practice from the program to benefit their
      lives with more happiness and prosperity.
    </p>
    <p>
      In the program, all participants have the opportunity to learn about the Theravada Buddhist monk's life, to train
      themselves with the Buddhist disciplines and Buddhist cultures, to practice meditation, to study a variety of
      Buddhist Dhamma topics, and to understand more about the Theravada Buddhist monk's life. The course of study in the
      program has been continuously well-developed from the beginning up until the present, by becoming more efficient
      in training those who are not raised as Buddhists, enabling them to learn and apply the teachings in this short
      period of time after the program is concluded.
    </p>
    <p>
      We therefore would like to invite all qualified persons for The Theravada-Monk Ordination to join the European
      Ordination Program again this year.
    </p>
    <h2>
      Registration
    </h2>
    <p>
      Qualifications for those who would like to join the program are:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Male between 18-70 years old</li>
      <li>A person with acceptable good behaviour as observed and can be attested to by their peers</li>
      <li>A person who lives a simple life, has good health, has no contagious diseases, mental illnesses, or physical
        impairments.
      </li>
      <li>A person who has no drug addictions or criminal records</li>
      <li>A written consent from a parent, guardian, spouse, or closest living relative is required for those who wish to
        join The European Ordination Program.
      </li>
      <li>Applicants requiring a guarantee letter for Europe must be vouched for by Dhammakaya Temple or one of its international branch temples i.e. by a monk or temple employee.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>
      Items Required to Join the Program
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>2 sets of white shirts and trousers</li>
      <li>1 standard white shirt used by The EU Dhammakaya branches ceremonies</li>
      <li>Sweaters</li>
      <li>1 towel</li>
      <li>Personal necessities such as soap, shampoo, toothpaste, and a toothbrush</li>
      <li>1 pair of sandals</li>
      <li>Any required medicine</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Items that are not allowed during the Training Program</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No dangerous sharp items that could be considered as weapons</li>
      <li>No cigarettes</li>
      <li>No valuable items</li>
      <li>No mobile phones</li>
      <li>No illegal drugs</li>
      <li>No food</li>
      <li>No music players, CD's, or radios</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Thank you for your interest in the European Ordination Program and we look forward to your participation.
    </p>
    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p>
      <Location />
    </p>
    <h2>Things to do before your arrival</h2>
    <p>
      You will need to memorise chanting text for the ordination ceremony:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/assets/docs/ordination-chanting.pdf">Download chanting texts</a></li>
    <!-- TODO finish chanting section
      <li><a href="/about/texts/#ordination-chanting-en">Online in English</a></li>
      <li><a href="/about/texts/#ordination-chanting-th">Online in Thai</a></li>
    -->
    </ul>
    <h2>Do you require a letter of guarantee for a visa?</h2>
    <p>
      If you require a letter from us to submit as part of your visa request, we ask you to find someone in our network of
      Dhammakaya temples who can vouch for you. This is our policy, because we want to prevent our program from being used
      as an excuse to stay in Europe illegally. If you don't know anyone in our network, you can find a Dhammakaya branch
      temple near you and an interview can be arranged.
    </p>
    <h2>Are you already a monk?</h2>
    <p>
      If you want to join the program, but you have already received the full ordination (upasampadā), and are currently
      still a monk, we cannot accept you in the program. We only accept lay people at the current moment.
    </p>
    <h2>How do I join?</h2>
    <p>
      Click on the button below and fill out the form to apply for the ordination program.<br>Note that this program is open to male participants only.
    </p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary d-inline-flex" href={FORM_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Apply
      &nbsp;
      <IconBoxArrowUpRight />
    </a>
    <div id="program-details--temples-in-europe" class="offset-anchor-for-fixed-nav"></div>
    <h1 class="text-center mt-5">Temples in Europe</h1>
    <div class="row">
      {templesByCountry.map(({ country, flag, temples }, index) => (
        <>
          <div class="col-12 px-3"><h4 class={index === 0 ? 'mb-0' : 'mb-0 mt-4'}>{flag} {country}</h4></div>
          {temples.map((temple) => (
            <div class="col-6 col-md-6 px-3">
              <Card title={temple.title} content={temple.content} />
            </div>
          ))}
        </>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
